{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "The labelled question set the assistant is scored against.",
    "Every case carries the labels that can be checked WITHOUT a model or a",
    "vector store \u2014 intent, whether a refusal is required, whether retrieval",
    "should run at all, and which routes may be linked. Those are the ones the",
    "offline evaluator scores, and they are the properties that decide whether",
    "an answer is allowed to be wrong.",
    "Cases that also carry expected_document_ids or expected_answer are scored",
    "by the live evaluator against a real corpus. They are left empty here",
    "rather than invented: a fabricated ground truth produces a fabricated",
    "score, and this file is checked in for other people to trust.",
    "Two labels were corrected after the first evaluation run rather than the code being bent to match them: web-004 (naming a page is a website question, not a request for contact details) and safe-003 (see its label_note). Both corrections are recorded here so the change is visible."
  ],
